<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernard Ato IV Trencavel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1129</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Bernard Aton IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernard Ato IV was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trencavel">Trencavel</a> family and viscount of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beziers">Béziers</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albi">Albi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimes">Nîmes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razes">Razès</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a>. Inheriting Carcassonne through his mother Ermengard, he built a principality between the rival counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, balancing between them. His descendants ruled from the walled city of Carcassonne until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernard-ato-iv-trencavel.jpg" alt="Bernard Ato IV Trencavel" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariage_of_Ermengard_of_Carcassonne_and_Gausfred_III_of_Roussillon.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
